{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/820831-spears-are-not-2-pawed-weapons","id":820831,"title":"Spears are not 2-Pawed weapons!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-01T01:29:32-08:00","id":820831,"title":"Spears are not 2-Pawed weapons!","content":"Seriously,<br /> <br /> I have no idea HOW this came to be considered fact back with D&amp;D 3.X, but a Spear is not primarily a weapon that requires 2-hands to wield properly. There is a reason why the primary weapon of most armies in the Early Medieval Period (aka Dark Ages) was a Spear. It was a simple weapon that the Peasants could wield along with a shield. Shieldwall tactics required the use of interlocked shields and a literal thicket of spears presented to the front of an enemy force. Now, a Spear COULD be wielded with 2-hands in such a way as either Thrusting/Piercing like with a Shieldwall. However, it could also be used as a Hewing weapon (in fact, a Hewing Spear has a longer blade that is sharpened and differentiated from the traditional thrusting spear).<br /> <br /> Could someone PLEASE fix this. There is a style of combat that is Spear/Shield that is every bit as logical and capable as Sword/Axe/Mace and Shield.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1801-craftmason-bob-s-cousin","name":"Craftmason Bob's Cousin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T12:31:30-08:00","id":821136,"title":"","content":"This goes back well before D&amp;D 3.X<br /> <br /> When most RPGs say &quot;spear&quot; they really mean, &quot;Two handed thrusting pole-arm.&quot;<br /> <br /> Usually making an appropriate one-handed, or mixed, spear is simple enough in most systems.<br /> <br /> Though a bit of a nitpick: a lot of shield wall formations did not have the front wall use spears. The front line(s) usually didn't even bother drawing a weapon, or used short swords, to focus on holding the wall, while a secondary line that wasn't part of the wall itself used spears to attack via the extra reach.<br /> <br /> It's not just that spears are simple weapons to learn to use (so are axes), but they allow infantry formations to multitask by having a mixed line with shields handling position control/defense, and spears handling offense.<br /> <br /> Solo shield and spear is actually not all that common in our historical record, and let's face it, Pugmire isn't really designed for large army formation tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T16:24:02-08:00","id":821290,"title":"","content":"Forgetting large army formation tactics, the spear was a common weapon of the individual viking. You'd best believe they one handed that mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T19:17:52-08:00","id":821371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craftmason Bob's Cousin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/820831-spears-are-not-2-pawed-weapons#post820831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously,<br /> <br /> I have no idea HOW this came to be considered fact back with D&amp;D 3.X,</div> </div> </div> </div>Just checked the 3.5 PHB. Shortspear is a Simple 1-handed weapon with a throwing range.<br /> <br /> Longspear's 2h though. Can't be thrown either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T04:33:56-08:00","id":821540,"title":"","content":"Worth noting that in D&amp;D 5e, which is effectively the basis for Pugmire, a spear is a 1-handed versatile weapon, which means you can 2-hand it for a bigger damage die. It also comes with a throwing range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:38:24-08:00","id":821720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/820831-spears-are-not-2-pawed-weapons?p=821371#post821371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just checked the 3.5 PHB. Shortspear is a Simple 1-handed weapon with a throwing range.</div> </div> </div> </div>I double checked the Pugmire Early Access file, and it seems to do the same thing but with javelins and spears, instead of short spears and long spears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T13:41:49-08:00","id":821857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/820831-spears-are-not-2-pawed-weapons?p=821720#post821720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I double checked the Pugmire Early Access file, and it seems to do the same thing but with javelins and spears, instead of short spears and long spears.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is consistent with DnD 5e, which is what Pugmire is based on. (Not arguing, just noting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}